blankpages@gmail.com (essej) writes:
> we're trying to find (or compose, i suppose) a definitive list of
> character class differences and abilities because we have some
> questions we can't find the answers to.

abil-343.txt is a list of abilities; it doesn't try to be a list of
differences, however.

> for example, are any classes blocked from casting certain classes of
> magic?

Not outright, no. However, some are better, or have the capability to
be better, than others in particular spell schools. See spl1-343.txt
for the full discussion.

> do any classes have spellcasting benefits?

Yes. spl1-343.txt lists the role-based spellcasting modifiers, and the
minor perks of being a Wizard.

> are any classes prohibited from using certain weapon types?

No; again, some have the capability of being better than others. See
weap-343.txt. (Some roles _are_ prohibited from using two weapons at
the same time.)

> if you're a priest(ess),
> does wisdom act as your spellcasting success/hunger adjusting
> attribute?

Spellcasting success, yes. The amount of hunger caused doesn't depend
on stats, only the spell level, except for Wizards.

